 {:db/id "q-125549" :question/id #uuid "8b30b956-8f97-5e5a-bc88-28b6d6148226" :question/math-academy-id "q-125549" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $2\\times 2$ matrix?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $P$ has $2$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 2.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $Q$ has $4$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $4\\times 2.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $R$ has $2$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 2.$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $R$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-125549/ma-source-field/7d9024f55c08fae807a40823aeed2806ecf0054c8c7dfff0023de16afb00288c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
