 {:db/id "q-125611" :question/id #uuid "a14b13fa-47dd-5e1a-8086-20e6009f70ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-125611" :question/problem "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $Y$ given below. Describe it in terms of ${y}_{ij}.$\n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry lies at the intersection of the $4$th row and $2$nd column. Hence, we have ${y}_{42}=7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125611/ma-source-field/6eaf9efb4526ff0bce0159645d0422c489bcbcc45dbd0d521dfc3d896f856db0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
