 {:db/id "q-126222" :question/id #uuid "8674af78-bd5e-58b6-917b-e86f01702cc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-126222" :question/problem "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0\\text{ }\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- $P$ is *not* a diagonal matrix since it's not a square matrix.\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a diagonal matrix since it's not a square matrix.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. But some of the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are not zeros (for instance, ${r}_{31}=7\\ne 0$).\n\nTherefore, none of the given are diagonal matrices." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126222/ma-source-field/8e644b44c7bdedc7f919a3ec5942e992837004a7ab7cd0978aa947c767b27356"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
