 {:db/id "q-126278" :question/id #uuid "b1fe65ee-e4c1-507a-9313-0ea6b012c1aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-126278" :question/problem "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- $A$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $1$ row and $1$ column, so it is a $1\\times 1$ matrix.\n\n- $B$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $3$ rows and $3$ columns, so it is a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- $C$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $1$ row and $2$ columns, so it's a $1\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are square matrices." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126278/ma-source-field/22d2ac77d77b67418cfdafd7ba6bf14b42a43fc51d9b68f5801313edbf38ea3c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
