 {:db/id "q-126774/ma-source-field/defa182d6a70cd8dea1c545a0bdde93e825c6c5750ef024b14942c370ec29f97" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e1c6021-571a-58eb-ae1a-ae2e4f0fcf7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-126774/ma-source-field/defa182d6a70cd8dea1c545a0bdde93e825c6c5750ef024b14942c370ec29f97/65530288e15328122e9d0954dc2ee73392f91237a3cade2b053eff6a41f1242d" "q-126774/ma-source-field/defa182d6a70cd8dea1c545a0bdde93e825c6c5750ef024b14942c370ec29f97/f6d9147d8d3636e624ec2333fa1af2e279178ce1fa743f9dcebed7acbfa983cc" "q-126774/ma-source-field/defa182d6a70cd8dea1c545a0bdde93e825c6c5750ef024b14942c370ec29f97/eae888614665477d74433604928a8e89963cafe9b30888ae386d1dead524400f" "q-126774/ma-source-field/defa182d6a70cd8dea1c545a0bdde93e825c6c5750ef024b14942c370ec29f97/0ac26ccbf4ceb7dcc9a98f01041b75e85c0aba1e02369d216e6a494a8208cdec" "q-126774/ma-source-field/defa182d6a70cd8dea1c545a0bdde93e825c6c5750ef024b14942c370ec29f97/d162e2faaec17b1a260170a7987e0140c78204a2643526769658c8819c3f8edd"] :answer-field/correct "q-126774/ma-source-field/defa182d6a70cd8dea1c545a0bdde93e825c6c5750ef024b14942c370ec29f97/d162e2faaec17b1a260170a7987e0140c78204a2643526769658c8819c3f8edd" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-126774" :question/id #uuid "e567d72e-c85f-58b7-9ff5-c8e3c41c5382" :question/math-academy-id "q-126774" :question/problem "Find the interval of convergence for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{3}^{n}{x}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}}=\\frac{3x}{{1}^{3/2}}-\\frac{{3}^{2}{x}^{2}}{{2}^{3/2}}+\\frac{{3}^{3}{x}^{3}}{{3}^{3/2}}-\\frac{{3}^{4}{x}^{4}}{{4}^{3/2}}+⋯\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To apply the ratio test we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{3}^{n}{x}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(-1)^{n+2}{3}^{n+1}{x}^{n+1}}{(n+1)^{3/2}}\\cdot \\frac{{n}^{3/2}}{(-1)^{n+1}{3}^{n}{x}^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{-3x{n}^{3/2}}{(n+1)^{3/2}}| \\\\  & =3|-x|\\cdot {lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{n}{n+1})}^{3/2} \\\\  & =3|x|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3|x|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ In this case, the convergence condition is satisfied for $|x|<\\frac{1}{3}.$ So, the radius of convergence is $\\frac{1}{3},$ and the series converges for any $x$ that lies in the open interval $(-\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{1}{3}).$\n\nThe ratio test gives no conclusion about the convergence of the series when $L=1.$ So, when $|x|=\\frac{1}{3},$ we do not know if the series converges. This means that the endpoints $x=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ need to be investigated separately using another test for convergence.\n\n- When $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{3}^{n}{x}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{3}^{n}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{(\\frac{3}{3})}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{2}^{3/2}}+\\frac{1}{{3}^{3/2}}-\\frac{1}{{4}^{3/2}}+⋯\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is convergent by the alternating series test.   So the endpoint $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ is included in our interval.\n\n- When $x=-\\frac{1}{3}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{3}^{n}{x}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{3}^{n}{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}(-1)^{n}{(\\frac{3}{3})}^{n}}{{n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{2n+1}}{{n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-(1+\\frac{1}{{2}^{3/2}}+\\frac{1}{{3}^{3/2}}+\\frac{1}{{4}^{3/2}}+⋯)\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is convergent by the $p$-series test.   So the endpoint $x=-\\frac{1}{3}$ is included in our interval.\n\nTherefore, the interval of convergence is $[-\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{1}{3}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126774/ma-source-field/defa182d6a70cd8dea1c545a0bdde93e825c6c5750ef024b14942c370ec29f97"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
