 {:db/id "q-126841/ma-source-field/16d672fbe6cd397f266f506d1e3f64195658ed63d59fb6bc6e7904c28a8af91c" :answer-field/id #uuid "19d09d6d-fdd3-564f-8577-1f47d907f393" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-126841/ma-source-field/16d672fbe6cd397f266f506d1e3f64195658ed63d59fb6bc6e7904c28a8af91c/ea0b6508e68821b37ec3651cab97c0fc80d9d531c1f449a5ade38cfacdcc34ee" "q-126841/ma-source-field/16d672fbe6cd397f266f506d1e3f64195658ed63d59fb6bc6e7904c28a8af91c/40c245253427ad7c193be2bb7e2474c08c0f8c4caeb1305385e566671fb049c0" "q-126841/ma-source-field/16d672fbe6cd397f266f506d1e3f64195658ed63d59fb6bc6e7904c28a8af91c/b2b9d3c1f4bbad2432847cb9d8e613a614550e96543e756c8493aae57694da49" "q-126841/ma-source-field/16d672fbe6cd397f266f506d1e3f64195658ed63d59fb6bc6e7904c28a8af91c/b74ef4dfa9b46b543f081479118871bb71c6fe75fc2b1601073c80b5e227bdd6" "q-126841/ma-source-field/16d672fbe6cd397f266f506d1e3f64195658ed63d59fb6bc6e7904c28a8af91c/35de2ed710b69784cc2e5fb5c0353f752ea8f27c6581dd3a1f12c5f8dbc98036"] :answer-field/correct "q-126841/ma-source-field/16d672fbe6cd397f266f506d1e3f64195658ed63d59fb6bc6e7904c28a8af91c/b2b9d3c1f4bbad2432847cb9d8e613a614550e96543e756c8493aae57694da49" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-126841" :question/id #uuid "1276b48a-33df-5447-9033-1c8e5ee23a8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-126841" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1),1-5t⟩$ at the point where $t=0,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "At the point where $t=0,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(0)+u{r}^{′}(0),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({0}^{2}+1),1-5(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-5t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1},-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\frac{2(0)}{{0}^{2}+1},-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨0,1⟩+u⟨0,-5⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126841/ma-source-field/16d672fbe6cd397f266f506d1e3f64195658ed63d59fb6bc6e7904c28a8af91c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
 {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60e28b26-0eb7-51ed-bcf9-2660b98a6028"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126841"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-126844/ma-source-field/db8a5f2ec52d8bdcf445fdc56b2d6713764a5a2fb6de2b0cd11255c8767543da/dc2ca9b2661cf4f56684318a465f5faeb9d871ad02746daf18a36237b4420eb7" :answer/id #uuid "49ec3922-a5e3-5d3a-8e40-816bba0da596" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+(x-2)-\\frac{1}{3}(x-2)^{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-126844/ma-source-field/db8a5f2ec52d8bdcf445fdc56b2d6713764a5a2fb6de2b0cd11255c8767543da/a23c3e231b6dbe47b42b39ba23b63edbb642eed231aeb4faa785e794b884533e" :answer/id #uuid "c59d759c-090a-569e-a841-2f3f881a6cf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)-\\frac{1}{4}(x-2)^{2}+⋯" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
