 {:db/id "q-126999" :question/id #uuid "6c2ff5db-c36f-5915-b1bd-10b9fa08582d" :question/math-academy-id "q-126999" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-9t \\\\ y=-2+7t \\\\ z=-8t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5-9t \\\\ -2+7t \\\\ -8t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-9t \\\\ 7t \\\\ -8t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126999/ma-source-field/ef9a23096c14509a38dbe00890bb0d7ce1e274bb970566254da5922b4963def7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
