 {:db/id "q-127002" :question/id #uuid "36cc5d87-ef5c-5ced-b253-0194de848513" :question/math-academy-id "q-127002" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=13-8t \\\\ y=7t \\\\ z=-7-3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13-8t \\\\ 7t \\\\ -7-3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-8t \\\\ 7t \\\\ -3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127002/ma-source-field/464625c0180dffcb5971301d1ecec5105d22cae444075f3562c610b25a920c34"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
