 {:db/id "q-127373" :question/id #uuid "38dbfb09-c609-5f82-9c41-6942da640f6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127373" :question/problem "A deck contains $10$ cards labeled with the numbers $4$, $7$, $10,…,31.$ If one card is randomly drawn from the deck, what is its expected value?" :question/worked-solution "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S={4,7,10,…,31},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{10}:$\n\n$$\nf(4)=f(7)=f(10)=…=f(31)=\\frac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =4\\cdot f(4)+7\\cdot f(7)+10\\cdot f(10)+…+31\\cdot f(10) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{10}+\\frac{7}{10}+\\frac{10}{10}+…+\\frac{31}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+7+10+13+16+19+22+25+28+31}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{175}{10} \\\\  & =17.5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127373/ma-source-field/c77195364db9dca36fafe389247052a6dc23baa4ecc6a34387ca8c2fca9762c9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
