 {:db/id "q-127826" :question/id #uuid "dd3729c7-43c0-5883-808f-5b63c7f7af84" :question/math-academy-id "q-127826" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-3\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 15=-30.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=7\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ does not have an inverse." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127826/ma-source-field/ff37df3206aa0faa4d5ea80472bb3f198d0e841838aacd2d11a9fcd844541838"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
