 {:db/id "q-128519/ma-source-field/d09cb344900a120046809497cfb6da5d5a3a7fc636e7d1d7336beec4e15188b6" :answer-field/id #uuid "975890c9-a5ad-56b9-8079-273dba5ca847" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-128519/ma-source-field/d09cb344900a120046809497cfb6da5d5a3a7fc636e7d1d7336beec4e15188b6/2f442747d0bc106b57897625554ad6b5fc20dcef083baa2e7348b04dfc2a50cf" "q-128519/ma-source-field/d09cb344900a120046809497cfb6da5d5a3a7fc636e7d1d7336beec4e15188b6/e25f1b67f7deae0637d318d7b4bbb78a171e2ac1da12c7f58e560e4d9db6ee6a" "q-128519/ma-source-field/d09cb344900a120046809497cfb6da5d5a3a7fc636e7d1d7336beec4e15188b6/c5527de6ce74e4f6712a423bed22be076a78a659bd412d2fed0d46a12d044b94" "q-128519/ma-source-field/d09cb344900a120046809497cfb6da5d5a3a7fc636e7d1d7336beec4e15188b6/0fccfb35ef4b926229e15a3cf49eee186d8705a4ff50f2dabf2e10635b9b6a2e" "q-128519/ma-source-field/d09cb344900a120046809497cfb6da5d5a3a7fc636e7d1d7336beec4e15188b6/ee10dc09bd178ececa8a1f8adf31e2392105cd6fbbd62cdc2900fbae89da64d1"] :answer-field/correct "q-128519/ma-source-field/d09cb344900a120046809497cfb6da5d5a3a7fc636e7d1d7336beec4e15188b6/2f442747d0bc106b57897625554ad6b5fc20dcef083baa2e7348b04dfc2a50cf" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-128519" :question/id #uuid "a633d445-62c8-5864-b7bf-d694cd1cd56c" :question/math-academy-id "q-128519" :question/problem "Given that $g(x,y)=\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x,$ find the points $(x,y)$ where $∇g(x,y)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y)=(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1)i-(\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{y})j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇g(x,y)=0:$\n\n$$\n(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1)i-(\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x})j=0\\,i+0\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1=0 \\\\ \\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{{(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ 9\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{81}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{81+3{x}^{3}}{{x}^{4}} & =0 \\\\ 81+3{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =-27 \\\\ x & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3,$ we get $y=-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{3}=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $∇g(x,y)=0$ at the point: $(-3,-3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128519/ma-source-field/d09cb344900a120046809497cfb6da5d5a3a7fc636e7d1d7336beec4e15188b6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
