 {:db/id "q-129129" :question/id #uuid "10f47672-b02f-5835-a498-94f2d2a69a14" :question/math-academy-id "q-129129" :question/problem "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and  $y$,  the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x+8y=6 \\\\ 4x+y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy simplifying, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8y=6 \\\\ 4x+y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129129/ma-source-field/4bc3df73cdcabeff9fafb859463c69ba6d232268e16385a8cad5bfef08bb25ba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
 {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7c8f4da-c782-51e0-ac51-87a89f31860d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129129"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}
