 {:db/id "q-129231" :question/id #uuid "3d92198e-4ce7-5520-a0eb-698c6d6eae5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129231" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are **not** in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129231/ma-source-field/29b29f0d99023720d6882665e8a9cdcd5df29c4db1f4c9a460aa90d37773c55a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
